cyberpunk 2077 fans are asking for cloud  saves on stadia and other developers are  reacting to the news of the service  coming to an end  if you missed it Google announced its  Cloud streaming service stadia will  officially be shut down on January 18  2023 all stadia Hardware purchases made  through the Google Store will be  refunded including games and add-on  content purchased from that specific  storefront cyberpunk 2077 is one of  those games that has been available to  Stevia Gamers since launch but with the  services looming Doom that means lots of  fans may have to start their journey in  nice city all over again over on the  stadia subreddit one user asked CD  projekt Red to add Cloud saves to the  stadia version of cyberpunk and added  quote I care more about my saved game  than a game refund other members of the  community came to the rescue suggesting  the use of Google takeout a service that  allows users to grab data off of  Google's services this would allow  players to download the save files and  import them into steam or Gog there are  a number of replies in the thread  confirming that this method works but  there are also a good handful of users  that are having trouble with the  workaround as stadia was failing to show  up in their takeout menu at the time of  this recording there is no word from  cdpr about the possibility of cloud  saves for stadia's version of cyberpunk  but January is still a couple months  away so anything can happen for now if  you happen to be dealing with this issue  keep giving Google takeout a try with  your fingers crossed meanwhile other  developers are taking steps to help make  sure stadia Gamers have a smooth  transition away from the platform for  example IO interactive tweeted quote to  all our Hitman fans on Google stadia we  hear you we are looking into ways for  you to continue your Hitman experience  on other platforms Ubisoft also reacted  to the news of stadia's demise and are  offering PC versions of stadia games to  purchasers in a statement Ubisoft said  quote while stadia will shut down on  January 18 2023 we are happy to share  that we are currently working to bring  the games you own on stadia to PC  through Ubisoft connect we'll have more  to share regarding specific details as  well as the impact for Ubisoft plus  subscribers at a later date and with  stadia's doom on the horizon you might  be wondering what cloud service you  should try out next the obvious choice  is Xbox but if you're an Amazon Prime  member you have access to a couple of  games each month that you can play for  no additional fee on Amazon's Cloud  platform Luna October's editions have  been recently announced and they're  worth a peek Metro Exodus might be the  most enticing game of the bunch offering  a horrific post-apocalyptic world to  explore you'll play as a Survivor that's  seeking refuge in the tunnels below  Moscow before heading out to find  greener pastures and start anew if  you're looking for something a bit  lighter you can enjoy skateboard this  month this quirky Indie has you zipping  around as a bird on a skateboard racking  up points by stringing together Combos  and completing a variety of challenges  on each stage other games in the October  Prime gaming channel lineup include the  iconic platformer earthworm gym 2  nightmare and using Blair Witch and  monster truck Championship hit the  comments and let me know your thoughts  on cloud gaming in general and we'll see  you next week
 

